[0.025, "o", "\r\n# Case: commit-whole-refactor  with 0.5  without 0.5\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "Based on your changes to the config module and README, here are the shell commands to commit:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit add src/config/loader.rs src/config/env.rs README.md\r\ngit commit -m \"Refactor config loader\r\n\r\n- Restructure config/loader.rs for improved maintainability\r\n- Update config/env.rs with refactored interface\r\n- Update README.md with changes\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf you'd prefer a different commit message format or style, let me know and I can adjust it.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "I don't have access to your repo or any CLAUDE.md guidelines, so I'll provide a clean, standard commit message. Adjust as needed for your project's conventions:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\ngit add src/config/loader.rs src/config/env.rs README.md\r\ngit commit -m \"Refactor config loader module\r\n\r\n- Restructure loader.rs for improved clarity and maintainability\r\n- Update env.rs to align with new architecture\r\n- Update README.md documentation\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf your project has specific commit message conventions (like a prefix or different format), let me know and I'll adjust it.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: jj-colocated-push  with 1  without 0\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "I need your commit message to complete this. What should the commit message be? (e.g., \"fix: parser handles nested expressions correctly\", \"fix: resolve infinite loop in tokenizer\", etc.)\r\n\r\nIn the meantime, here's the command sequence once you provide the message:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\njj describe -m \"<YOUR_MESSAGE_HERE>\"\r\njj new\r\njj bookmark set fix-parser -r @-\r\njj push --bookmark fix-parser --remote origin\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe steps:\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "```bash\r\njj new -m \"Fix parser\"\r\njj branch set fix-parser\r\njj git push -b fix-parser\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis:\r\n1. Creates a new change from your working copy changes\r\n2. Names it with the branch `fix-parser`\r\n3. Pushes that branch to `origin`\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "\r\n# Case: open-deck-pull-request  with 0.6666666666666666  without 0\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## with the rune\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "```bash\r\ngh pr create --title \"fix: parser crash with empty frontmatter\" --body \"## Summary\r\n\r\n- Fixes a crash that occurs when a rune has empty frontmatter\r\n- Parser now handles empty frontmatter sections gracefully\r\n\r\n## Release Notes\r\n\r\nParser no longer crashes when processing runes with empty frontmatter.\"\r\n```\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "## without the rune\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "I don't see a CLAUDE.md documenting your PR discipline, and I don't have it in my memory yet. I need to know your conventions for the PR title and body format before I generate the exact command.\r\n\r\nWhat does your PR discipline specify? For example:\r\n- Title format (e.g., scope: description, or just description)?\r\n- Body sections (e.g., description, testing notes, breaking changes)?\r\n- Any other conventions?\r\n\r\nOr if you'd like, just tell me the title and body you want, and I'll give you the `gh` command.\r\n"]
